course: dictionary
lesson: 14056
title: Marvellous and wonder
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Marvellous» is a happy word. It means extremely good, wonderful. «We had a marvellous day at the seaside.» The clues are the day and the seaside: a day at the seaside is fun, so marvellous means wonderful. Ask yourself what word would fit, then try your meaning in the sentence.
explain: The dictionary also gives an old use: causing great wonder or surprise. «The magician pulled a bird out of his hat, and the whole crowd gasped.» The gasping shows the trick was so amazing that people were surprised. Marvellous is a little old-fashioned or posh, so you may meet it in old stories.
explain: In The Wind in the Willows, Toad calls everything marvellous when he is excited. In Alice's Adventures in Wonderland, Alice finds marvellous things. Look at the words around marvellous in these books: they show you the feeling, which is wonder and delight.
fact: «Marvellous» means extremely good, wonderful.
fact: The old use of «marvellous» means causing great wonder or surprise, or amazing.
fact: British, Irish, Australian and New Zealand English spell it marvellous, with two l's. American English spells it marvelous, with one l.
fact: «Marvellous» can describe a day, a thing, a person or a feeling: «a marvellous day», «a marvellous idea».
fact: Toad in The Wind in the Willows says marvellous when he is excited, so the word often shows a happy, excited mood.
exercise: «We had a marvellous day at the seaside.» What does marvellous mean here? | *Extremely good, wonderful | Cold and wet | Long and boring | Very quiet
exercise: Toad calls everything marvellous when he is excited. What feeling does the word show? | Sleepy | *Excited and happy | Angry | Bored
exercise: Which spelling of marvellous is used in American English? | marvellus | marvelus | *marvelous | marvellouss
test: «The magician's trick was marvellous, and the crowd gasped.» What does marvellous mean in this sentence? | Sad | Boring | *Wonderful and amazing | Dirty
test: Alice finds marvellous things in Wonderland. What does marvellous suggest about those things? | Ordinary and dull | Frightening and cruel | Small and dark | *Amazing and full of wonder
exam: Which word could replace marvellous in «a marvellous day» without changing the meaning? | *Wonderful | Late | Dull | Rainy
